{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHezLMoBrRMeG3JoFJQeVo","type":"tool_result","content":"312\t    return None, None, caps[-1] if caps else None\n313\t\n314\t\n315\tdef norm(s):\n316\t    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]\", \"\", (s or \"\").lower())\n317\t\n318\t\n319\t# card 127-2 (PD255(a) carry; review archive/peer/2026-10-01-c126-4-elocr.md:73): OCR reads 'SubVI' as 'subvl' and\n320\t# 'anything' as 'anvthing'. ADD-ONLY: norm() is unchanged (expected files store its keys); norm_ocr() is the alias-folded\n321\t# form, applied to BOTH sides only where a caller opts in (_hit's fallback, class_counts(ocr=True)).\n322\tOCR_ALIASES = ((\"vl\", \"vi\"), (\"v\", \"y\"))\n323\t\n324\t\n325\tdef ocr_fold(k):\n326\t    for a, b in OCR_ALIASES:\n327\t        k = k.replace(a, b)\n328\t    return k\n329\t\n330\t\n331\tdef norm_ocr(s):\n332\t    return ocr_fold(norm(s))\n333\t\n334\t\n335\t# EXPECTED ERRORS FROM THE PLAN (card chat-E2): a staged bed is broken BY DESIGN - its plan\n336\t# (tools/bench/plan_<stage>*.json, schema stageplan/1) declares `open_rows` [{node, term, why}] left for a later\n337\t# stage. Each open row licenses the Error List items LabVIEW raises for it, derived per node class from the plan's\n338\t# base graph (`base.path` objs[].class): a SubVI -> \"... '<term>' is not wired\" (only REQUIRED inputs are listed,\n339\t# so the licence is not required to appear); any other node -> one \"Contains unwired or bad terminal\"; and the\n340\t# half-wires an open row leaves -> the wire classes in WIRE_CLASSES. Their COUNT is not derivable from open_rows\n341\t# (one deleted sink can leave loose ends on several branches), so the wire licence is class-level and uncapped;\n342\t# the JSON records how many items it absorbed. Anything no licence covers is `extra` -> MISMATCH.\n343\tWIRE_CLASSES = (\"wirehaslooseends\", \"hasnosource\", \"outputlooptunneltoaninput\", \"twoterminalsofdifferenttypes\")\n344\t# REVERTED by docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md Pre-decided 195(b) (cycle 88): cycle 87's uncapped additions\n345\t# \"isnotconnectedtoanything\" and \"zerosources\" are removed - an uncapped class licence hides a real fault of the same\n346\t# wording (archive/peer/2026-09-26-c87-errorlist-extras.md:118). The L2-A1 bed's items are licensed instead by an\n347\t# explicit, exact-count file: tools/bench/errorlist_expected_D1_l2_a1_20260925_235224.json.\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tdef plan_for_bed(bed, bench=None):\n351\t    \"\"\"stage_d1_<s>.json whose `work` is this bed -> the stageplan plan_<s>*.json carrying open_rows.\"\"\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4a59a87-4d15-41da-99bd-766041ad1a3b","uuid":"925d0290-38da-4a54-96dd-7b96db2774c9","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:58:47.760Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"G:\\Codes\\LabVIEW_Codes\\MinLab\\zz_LabView VI\\AAA_UNIST\\2. Tracking\\V6_ParallelLoop\\tools\\errorlist_check.py","content":"    return None, None, caps[-1] if caps else None\n\n\ndef norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]\", \"\", (s or \"\").lower())\n\n\n# card 127-2 (PD255(a) carry; review archive/peer/2026-10-01-c126-4-elocr.md:73): OCR reads 'SubVI' as 'subvl' and\n# 'anything' as 'anvthing'. ADD-ONLY: norm() is unchanged (expected files store its keys); norm_ocr() is the alias-folded\n# form, applied to BOTH sides only where a caller opts in (_hit's fallback, class_counts(ocr=True)).\nOCR_ALIASES = ((\"vl\", \"vi\"), (\"v\", \"y\"))\n\n\ndef ocr_fold(k):\n    for a, b in OCR_ALIASES:\n        k = k.replace(a, b)\n    return k\n\n\ndef norm_ocr(s):\n    return ocr_fold(norm(s))\n\n\n# EXPECTED ERRORS FROM THE PLAN (card chat-E2): a staged bed is broken BY DESIGN - its plan\n# (tools/bench/plan_<stage>*.json, schema stageplan/1) declares `open_rows` [{node, term, why}] left for a later\n# stage. Each open row licenses the Error List items LabVIEW raises for it, derived per node class from the plan's\n# base graph (`base.path` objs[].class): a SubVI -> \"... '<term>' is not wired\" (only REQUIRED inputs are listed,\n# so the licence is not required to appear); any other node -> one \"Contains unwired or bad terminal\"; and the\n# half-wires an open row leaves -> the wire classes in WIRE_CLASSES. Their COUNT is not derivable from open_rows\n# (one deleted sink can leave loose ends on several branches), so the wire licence is class-level and uncapped;\n# the JSON records how many items it absorbed. Anything no licence covers is `extra` -> MISMATCH.\nWIRE_CLASSES = (\"wirehaslooseends\", \"hasnosource\", \"outputlooptunneltoaninput\", \"twoterminalsofdifferenttypes\")\n# REVERTED by docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md Pre-decided 195(b) (cycle 88): cycle 87's uncapped additions\n# \"isnotconnectedtoanything\" and \"zerosources\" are removed - an uncapped class licence hides a real fault of the same\n# wording (archive/peer/2026-09-26-c87-errorlist-extras.md:118). The L2-A1 bed's items are licensed instead by an\n# explicit, exact-count file: tools/bench/errorlist_expected_D1_l2_a1_20260925_235224.json.\n\n\ndef plan_for_bed(bed, bench=None):\n    \"\"\"stage_d1_<s>.json whose `work` is this bed -> the stageplan plan_<s>*.json carrying open_rows.\"\"\"","numLines":40,"startLine":312,"totalLines":768}}}
